hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15426","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Imran, a man who was at Wasit, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza narrating, from his father, that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not complete the takbir, meaning when he lowered and when he raised."
"15427","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, he said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating, from Zurarah, Hajjaj said in his hadith, he said: I heard Zurarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High."
"15428","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl and Zubayd al-Iyami, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O you disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. And when he saluted, he said: Glory be to the King, the Holy, Glory be to the King, the Holy, Glory be to the King, the Holy, and he raised his voice with it."
"15429","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Azrah, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He used to recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O you disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. And when he saluted, he said: Glory be to the King, the Holy, prolonging it three times."
"15430","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, he said: I heard Zurarah narrating, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O you disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. And when he saluted, he said: Glory be to the King, the Holy, saying it three times."
"15431","Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of this. He said: Zubayd and Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed me, both of them heard Dharr narrating, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of this."
"15432","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Zubayd and Salamah informed me that both of them heard Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O you disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. And when he saluted, he said: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times, raising his voice with the last of them."
"15433","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O you disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. And he said when he saluted: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times."
"15434","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Dharr, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: We have entered the morning upon the fitrah of Islam, and upon the word of sincerity, and upon the religion of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and upon the creed of our father Ibrahim, upright, Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists."
"15435","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Zubayd, from Dharr ibn Abd Allah al-Murhibi, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O you disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. And when he wanted to turn away from witr, he said: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times, then he raised his voice in the third."
"15436","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Dharr al-Hamdani, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza al-Khuzai, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say: O you disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. And he said when he sat at the end of his prayer: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times, prolonging his voice with the last."
"15437","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he entered the morning and when he entered the evening: We have entered the morning upon the fitrah of Islam, and upon the word of sincerity, and upon the religion of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and upon the creed of our father Ibrahim, upright, and he was not of the polytheists."
"15438","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shubah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Dharr, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: We have entered the morning upon the fitrah of Islam, and the word of sincerity, and the religion of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the creed of our father Ibrahim, upright, and he was not of the polytheists."
"15439","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from Dharr, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr and omitted a verse. So when he prayed, he said: Is Ubayy ibn Kab among the people? Ubayy said: O Messenger of Allah, was such-and-such verse abrogated, or did you forget it? He said: I was made to forget it."
"15440","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Zurarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High."
"15441","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the morning, said: We have entered the morning upon the fitrah of Islam, and the word of sincerity, and the religion of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the creed of our father Ibrahim, upright, and he was not of the polytheists."
"15442","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Abu Said al-Khuzai, from Ibn Abza, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to point with his forefinger in prayer."
"15443","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Imran, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, that he prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not complete the takbir."
"15444","Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rashid Abu Sad, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sat in prayer and supplicated, placed his right hand upon his thigh, then he pointed with his finger."
"15445","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Abd Allah ibn al-Qasim, he said: We sat with Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, so he said: Shall I not show you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: So we said: Yes indeed. He said: So he stood and said takbir, then recited, then bowed and placed his hands upon his knees until every limb took its place. Then he raised until every limb took its place. Then he prostrated until every limb took its place. Then he raised until every bone took its place. Then he prostrated until every bone took its place. Then he raised and did in the second rakah as he did in the first rakah. Then he said: Thus is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
